- Configure basic WordPress installation
- Implement basic theme structure

### Phase 2: Core Functionality
- Develop/customize theme
- Implement essential plugins
- Create content structure
- Set up SEO foundations
- Configure security measures

### Phase 3: Advanced Features
- Implement e-commerce (if applicable)
- Develop custom post types
- Create user management system
- Set up analytics
- Optimize performance

### Phase 4: Refinement
- User testing and feedback
- Performance optimization
- Security hardening
- Content polishing
- Final quality assurance

### Phase 5: Launch and Maintenance
- Production deployment
- Monitoring setup
- Backup system implementation
- Update schedule establishment
- Documentation finalization

## Maintenance Plan
- Weekly plugin updates
- Monthly theme updates
- Quarterly security audits
- Bi-annual performance reviews
- Regular content updates
- Daily automated backups

## Success Metrics
- Website uptime (target: 99.9%)
- Page load speed (target: < 2 seconds)
- Mobile usability score (target: > 90%)
- Conversion rates (specific to site goals)
- SEO rankings for target keywords
- User engagement metrics

## Shortlinks Service
The cFish.io ecosystem includes a dedicated shortlink service hosted at u.cfish.io that provides quick access to key documentation and information.

### Shortlink Management
- Shortlinks are maintained in markdown files and deployed to the live site
- Each shortlink has standardized metadata including URL, last updated date, purpose, and target audience
- AI-optimized JSON versions of each shortlink are maintained in the `/shortlinks/json/` directory
- Follow standard WordPress development workflow for shortlink content changes

### Available Shortlinks
- [cFish](https://u.cfish.io/cfish) - Documentation for cFish.io operational procedures
- [cFish IT](https://u.cfish.io/cfish-it) - Technical support and troubleshooting procedures
- [tY](https://u.cfish.io/ty) - Personal and professional profile for tY FischEYe

## Emergency Protocols
The following emergency protocols are established for system issues:

### Platform Integration Emergency Protocol
- System issues are categorized by priority level (RED, AMBER, GREEN)
- RED issues require immediate Tech Lead alert and system-wide health check
- AMBER issues require 30-minute DMT Team alert and data integrity checks
- GREEN issues require 2-hour Support Team alert and platform permission verification
- All issues are documented in Notion and monitored until resolution
- Unresolved issues are escalated to the next level

### Data Synchronization Troubleshooting
- Data mismatch issues trigger an alert to the DMT Team
- Data integrity checks are run to identify and document issues
- Platform status and integration points are verified
- System-wide health checks are performed when necessary

### Communication System Verification
- Communication issues are categorized by system type (Live Chat, AI Assistant, Video Conf)
- Direct testing is performed based on system type
- Unresolved issues are escalated to the Support Team
- All systems are verified after implementing fixes